winemac, win32u: Windows desktops and kiosk windows as overlay.
- Only the input desktop's windows are visible, as on Windows: win32u's NtUserSwitchDesktop
  calls the new user driver entry pSwitchDesktop (WINE_GDI_DRIVER_VERSION 109); winemac tells
  all processes of the prefix through a distributed notification, and each window knows its
  desktop. Kiosk/exam software that switches to its own desktop no longer shows its controller
  windows from the default desktop.
- With VIRTUAL_KIOSK_OVERLAY set (Virtual does that), windows of such a kiosk desktop and
  borderless full-screen windows stay above normal Mac apps even when another app is active,
  instead of a locked-down full-screen mode. The distributed notification
  "com.oezdek.virtual.kiosk" (Virtual's shortcut, default Option-Command-Z) shrinks large kiosk
  windows to 70 % at normal level and restores them. Normal windows are unaffected; no timers.
- macdrv_GetWindowStyleMasks no longer leaves ex_style_mask uninitialized.
Replaces an earlier version that polled every window and resized all windows.
